WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.960
In this sample learning application, the goal and next activity are saved with the work.

00:00:08.129 --> 00:00:11.644
Starting an activity first opens a review.

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:17.289
It names the activity and shows the exact change, from not started to in progress.

00:00:17.289 --> 00:00:19.921
Approve only when it matches your intent.

00:00:22.129 --> 00:00:27.513
After approval, StatePort applies the change and updates the learning state.

00:00:27.513 --> 00:00:30.039
The activity is now in progress.

00:00:30.039 --> 00:00:34.447
You can pause it, choose another activity, or write a reflection.

00:00:36.129 --> 00:00:39.039
A reflection starts as a browser draft.

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:43.592
Review its exact effect before saving it as evidence.

00:00:43.592 --> 00:00:46.684
StatePort keeps self-reported learning

00:00:46.684 --> 00:00:49.776
separate from independently verified progress.

00:00:51.129 --> 00:00:54.315
Open the receipt to inspect what StatePort applied.

00:00:54.315 --> 00:00:57.644
The recorded result belongs to this application.

00:00:57.644 --> 00:01:01.137
It provides a trail you can inspect, without

00:01:01.137 --> 00:01:04.631
treating a saved reflection as independently verified learning.

00:01:06.129 --> 00:01:12.026
After restarting the local service, the completed activity and reflection are still here.
